@.str.473 = private unnamed_addr constant [20 x i8] c"manage Nix profiles\00", align 1
@.str.474 = private unnamed_addr constant [5050 x i8] c"\0A\0A# Description\0A\0A`nix profile` allows you to create and manage *Nix profiles*. A Nix\0Aprofile is a set of packages that can be installed and upgraded\0Aindependently from each other. Nix profiles are versioned, allowing\0Athem to be rolled back easily.\0A\0A# Files\0A\0A\0A## Profiles\0A\0AA directory that contains links to profiles managed by [`nix-env`] and [`nix profile`]:\0A\0A- `$XDG_STATE_HOME/nix/profiles` for regular users\0A- `$NIX_STATE_DIR/profiles/per-user/root` if the user is `root`\0A\0AA profile is a directory of symlinks to files in the Nix store.\0A\0A### Filesystem layout\0A\0AProfiles are versioned as follows. When using a profile named *path*, *path* is a symlink to *path*`-`*N*`-link`, where *N* is the version of the profile.\0AIn turn, *path*`-`*N*`-link` is a symlink to a path in the Nix store.\0AFor example:\0A\0A```console\0A$ ls -l ~alice/.local/state/nix/profiles/profile*\0Alrwxrwxrwx 1 alice users 14 Nov 25 14:35 /home/alice/.local/state/nix/profiles/profile -> profile-7-link\0Alrwxrwxrwx 1 alice users 51 Oct 28 16:18 /home/alice/.local/state/nix/profiles/profile-5-link -> /nix/store/q69xad13ghpf7ir87h0b2gd28lafjj1j-profile\0Alrwxrwxrwx 1 alice users 51 Oct 29 13:20 /home/alice/.local/state/nix/profiles/profile-6-link -> /nix/store/6bvhpysd7vwz7k3b0pndn7ifi5xr32dg-profile\0Alrwxrwxrwx 1 alice users 51 Nov 25 14:35 /home/alice/.local/state/nix/profiles/profile-7-link -> /nix/store/mp0x6xnsg0b8qhswy6riqvimai4gm677-profile\0A```\0A\0AEach of these symlinks is a root for the Nix garbage collector.\0A\0AThe contents of the store path corresponding to each version of the\0Aprofile is a tree of symlinks to the files of the installed packages,\0Ae.g.\0A\0A```console\0A$ ll -R ~eelco/.local/state/nix/profiles/profile-7-link/\0A/home/eelco/.local/state/nix/profiles/profile-7-link/:\0Atotal 20\0Adr-xr-xr-x 2 root root 4096 Jan  1  1970 bin\0A-r--r--r-- 2 root root 1402 Jan  1  1970 manifest.nix\0Adr-xr-xr-x 4 root root 4096 Jan  1  1970 share\0A\0A/home/eelco/.local/state/nix/profiles/profile-7-link/bin:\0Atotal 20\0Alrwxrwxrwx 5 root root 79 Jan  1  1970 chromium -> /nix/store/ijm5k0zqisvkdwjkc77mb9qzb35xfi4m-chromium-86.0.4240.111/bin/chromium\0Alrwxrwxrwx 7 root root 87 Jan  1  1970 spotify -> /nix/store/w9182874m1bl56smps3m5zjj36jhp3rn-spotify-1.1.26.501.gbe11e53b-15/bin/spotify\0Alrwxrwxrwx 3 root root 79 Jan  1  1970 zoom-us -> /nix/store/wbhg2ga8f3h87s9h5k0slxk0m81m4cxl-zoom-us-5.3.469451.0927/bin/zoom-us\0A\0A/home/eelco/.local/state/nix/profiles/profile-7-link/share/applications:\0Atotal 12\0Alrwxrwxrwx 4 root root 120 Jan  1  1970 chromium-browser.desktop -> /nix/store/4cf803y4vzfm3gyk3vzhzb2327v0kl8a-chromium-unwrapped-86.0.4240.111/share/applications/chromium-browser.desktop\0Alrwxrwxrwx 7 root root 110 Jan  1  1970 spotify.desktop -> /nix/store/w9182874m1bl56smps3m5zjj36jhp3rn-spotify-1.1.26.501.gbe11e53b-15/share/applications/spotify.desktop\0Alrwxrwxrwx 3 root root 107 Jan  1  1970 us.zoom.Zoom.desktop -> /nix/store/wbhg2ga8f3h87s9h5k0slxk0m81m4cxl-zoom-us-5.3.469451.0927/share/applications/us.zoom.Zoom.desktop\0A\0A\E2\80\A6\0A```\0A\0AEach profile version contains a manifest file:\0A- [`manifest.nix`](@docroot@/command-ref/files/manifest.nix.md) used by [`nix-env`](@docroot@/command-ref/nix-env.md).\0A- [`manifest.json`](@docroot@/command-ref/files/manifest.json.md) used by [`nix profile`](@docroot@/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md) (experimental).\0A\0A## User profile link\0A\0AA symbolic link to the user's current profile:\0A\0A- `~/.nix-profile`\0A- `$XDG_STATE_HOME/nix/profile` if [`use-xdg-base-directories`] is set to `true`.\0A\0ABy default, this symlink points to:\0A\0A- `$XDG_STATE_HOME/nix/profiles/profile` for regular users\0A- `$NIX_STATE_DIR/profiles/per-user/root/profile` for `root`\0A\0AThe `PATH` environment variable should include `/bin` subdirectory of the profile link (e.g. `~/.nix-profile/bin`) for the user environment to be visible to the user.\0AThe [installer](@docroot@/installation/installing-binary.md) sets this up by default, unless you enable [`use-xdg-base-directories`].\0A\0A[`nix-env`]: @docroot@/command-ref/nix-env.md\0A[`nix profile`]: @docroot@/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md\0A[`use-xdg-base-directories`]: @docroot@/command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-use-xdg-base-directories\0A\0A\0A### Profile compatibility\0A\0A> **Warning**\0A>\0A> Once you have used [`nix profile`] you can no longer use [`nix-env`] without first deleting `$XDG_STATE_HOME/nix/profiles/profile`\0A\0A[`nix-env`]: @docroot@/command-ref/nix-env.md\0A[`nix profile`]: @docroot@/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md\0A\0AOnce you installed a package with [`nix profile`], you get the following error message when using [`nix-env`]:\0A\0A```console\0A$ nix-env -f '<nixpkgs>' -iA 'hello'\0Aerror: nix-env\0Aprofile '/home/alice/.local/state/nix/profiles/profile' is incompatible with 'nix-env'; please use 'nix profile' instead\0A```\0A\0ATo migrate back to `nix-env` you can delete your current profile:\0A\0A> **Warning**\0A>\0A> This will delete packages that have been installed before, so you may want to back up this information before running the command.\0A\0A```console\0A $ rm -rf \22${XDG_STATE_HOME-$HOME/.local/state}/nix/profiles/profile\22\0A```\0A\0A\00", align 1
